{
  "id": "q3-classification",
  "order": 3,
  "title": "Race Classification",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "statement": "Make the official results of the race.\n\nEach line gives one driver: their code followed by **all of their lap times** in milliseconds (every finisher did the same number of laps), or their code followed by `DNF` if they did not finish.\n\nA finisher's race time is the sum of their laps. Sort the finishers by race time, fastest first (equal times keep the order of the input).\n\n- The winner's line is `1 CODE H:MM:SS.mmm` (their total race time).\n- Every other finisher: `position CODE +S.mmm`, the gap to the winner in seconds with three decimals.\n- Then one line `DNF CODE` for each driver who did not finish, in input order.",
  "input_format": "Line 1: `n`, the number of drivers.\nThen `n` lines: `CODE t1 t2 … tm` or `CODE DNF`. At least one driver finished.",
  "output_format": "One line per finisher, then one line per DNF driver.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 24",
    "1 ≤ m ≤ 70",
    "60000 ≤ lap time ≤ 200000"
  ],
